# gRPC Testing Rules

## Unit Test Service Logic Directly
Test `internal/service/` with plain Go tests. Call service methods directly — no gRPC plumbing, no network, no generated server scaffolding. Inject mock repositories via interfaces.

```go
func TestGetUser(t *testing.T) {
    ctrl := gomock.NewController(t)
    defer ctrl.Finish()

    mockRepo := mocks.NewMockUserRepository(ctrl)
    svc := service.NewUserService(mockRepo)

    mockRepo.EXPECT().FindByID(gomock.Any(), "123").Return(&domain.User{ID: "123", Name: "Alice"}, nil)

    resp, err := svc.GetUser(context.Background(), &pb.GetUserRequest{Id: "123"})
    require.NoError(t, err)
    assert.Equal(t, "Alice", resp.User.Name)
}
```

## Integration Tests with bufconn
Use `google.golang.org/grpc/test/bufconn` to create an in-memory gRPC server. No real network, no ports, fast startup. Tag these `//go:build integration`.

```go
//go:build integration

func newTestServer(t *testing.T) (pb.UserServiceClient, func()) {
    lis := bufconn.Listen(1024 * 1024)
    s := grpc.NewServer()
    pb.RegisterUserServiceServer(s, service.NewUserService(testRepo))
    go s.Serve(lis)

    conn, _ := grpc.DialContext(context.Background(), "bufnet",
        grpc.WithContextDialer(func(ctx context.Context, _ string) (net.Conn, error) {
            return lis.DialContext(ctx)
        }),
        grpc.WithTransportCredentials(insecure.NewCredentials()),
    )

    return pb.NewUserServiceClient(conn), func() {
        conn.Close()
        s.Stop()
    }
}
```

## Table-Driven Tests
All test cases in `[]struct{name, input, wantErr}` format. No single-case test functions when multiple cases exist.

```go
tests := []struct {
    name    string
    input   *pb.GetUserRequest
    want    *pb.GetUserResponse
    wantErr codes.Code
}{
    {"found", &pb.GetUserRequest{Id: "123"}, &pb.GetUserResponse{...}, codes.OK},
    {"not found", &pb.GetUserRequest{Id: "999"}, nil, codes.NotFound},
    {"empty id", &pb.GetUserRequest{Id: ""}, nil, codes.InvalidArgument},
}
for _, tt := range tests {
    t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) { ... })
}
```

## Mock Dependencies
Generate mocks with `mockery` for all repository interfaces. Keep mocks in `internal/mocks/`. Never hand-write mocks.

```bash
mockery --name=UserRepository --dir=internal/repository --output=internal/mocks
```

## Proto Conformance
`buf breaking` in CI ensures no backwards-incompatible proto changes. This is a test gate, not just a lint gate — it blocks the merge if proto changes break existing clients.
